# No Cursor Co-authored-by in commits

## Do

- Commit messages: subject + optional body only.
- Strip any `Co-authored-by:` trailer that names Cursor / Cursor Agent or uses `cursoragent@cursor.com` before finishing a commit (and before push).
- After commit, verify with `git log -1 --format=%B`. If a Cursor trailer remains, rewrite the message (amend only when amend rules allow).

## Don’t

- Don’t add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`.
- Don’t add `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>`.
- Don’t leave historical Cursor co-author trailers on `master` / `origin/master`.

Other human `Co-authored-by:` lines may remain.
